# ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║              AUTO-DOCUMENTATION SYSTEM — HOW IT WORKS         ║
# ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
#
# On every push the GitHub Action (docgen.yml) walks all project files
# and recreates a mirror structure inside docs/:
#
#   src/app.php       ->  docs/src/app.php.md
#   src/utils/math.js ->  docs/src/utils/math.js.md
#   style.css         ->  docs/style.css.md
#
# Every folder inside docs/ gets a README.md — an index with links to all
# files and subfolders of that level.
#
# --- HOW TO ADD DOCUMENTATION ----------------------------------------------
#
# A file page (docs/<path>.md) is created ONCE, with a heading, and is never
# touched by the automation again. Write anywhere in it; no markers needed.
#
# The <!-- DOCGEN:START/END --> markers matter ONLY in folder README.md files:
# the block between them is regenerated, while text above START and below END
# is preserved.
#
# Example (docs/src/README.md):
#
#   <!-- DOCGEN:START -->
#   # src
#   ...generated index...
#   <!-- DOCGEN:END -->
#                             <- anything written here is kept forever
#   ## Description
#   Application entry point. Initializes the config and the router.
#
# --- HOW UPDATES WORK ------------------------------------------------------
#
# * New file in the repo   -> a matching .md is created (heading only)
# * File removed from repo -> its .md is removed too, empty folders pruned
# * Existing file page     -> never overwritten
# * README.md in folders   -> only the DOCGEN:START/END block is refreshed;
#                             if there are no markers, it is prepended
#
# --- HOW TO CONFIGURE FILTERING (.docignore) -------------------------------
#
# This file (.docignore) is a blacklist — list what to exclude.
# Supported forms (.gitignore syntax):
#
#   *.ext            - all files with the extension  (example: *.png)
#   dirname/         - the whole folder              (example: node_modules/)
#   filename         - a file by name, at any depth  (example: package-lock.json)
#   path/to/file     - path from the repo root       (example: src/app.js)
#   dir/*.js         - files in a folder, not nested (example: dist/*.js)
#   dir/**           - everything inside, recursive   (example: dist/**)
#   dir/**/*.js      - a mask at any depth            (example: dist/**/*.min.js)
#   *                - any characters except /        (example: build-*.log)
#   **               - any characters including /     (example: **/tmp)
#   ?                - one character except /         (example: file?.txt)
#   !pattern         - negate a previous rule         (example: !examples/)
#   # comment        - lines starting with # are ignored
#
# A pattern containing a slash is anchored to the repo root; without a slash
# it matches at any depth (as in .gitignore). Rules are applied in order and
# the last match wins. Matching is case-insensitive.
#
# The file is created automatically on the first run and never overwritten.
# Edit it freely — changes take effect on the next push.
# Note: once a file becomes excluded, its page in docs/ is deleted along with
# whatever text was written in it.
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
# Blacklist for docs generation
# Syntax: *.ext, dirname/, filename, !negation. Comments: #
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════

